ops.body:
Acted on the root a28fec0-handoff comment.
Pseudo-version pins: the cc-sync draft-PR Run wf_7aa48998-743 already pins go.mod to the FINAL PUSHED synckit (cc-sync/artifact-delivery) and reposync (cc-sync/worktree-snapshot, once it contains D15 448a6d3) commit SHAs via `go get @<sha>`. All gates run with GOWORK=off, so CI needs no local go.work. No intermediate releases or tags. The new-synckitd (>= v0.40.0) requirement is documented in the PR body and install preflight.
Real-process acceptance: SPECULATIVE Run wf_69d4edac-275, branch cc-sync/realproc, worktree /Users/yasyf/.claude/worktrees/cc-sync/realproc.
- (1) A read-only investigation with cites: label/plist/socket/state derivation and whether DAEMONKIT_HOME isolates them; foreground serve/helper and readiness signals; how the remote transport invokes ssh; host facts and discovery; the cc-sync install sequence and the probe race.
- (2) A `realproc`-tagged test package using the real synckitd built from the synckit final branch and the real cc-sync binary:
  - isolated hosts A and B (HOME/DAEMONKIT_HOME/XDG/state under temp);
  - foreground synckitd serve + cc-sync helper-serve with real readiness waits;
  - real CLI status/sync/list/pickup --json processes;
  - A→B delivery through the real remote transport via a PATH-injected ssh shim that routes into B's isolated env (only the ssh hop is simulated);
  - fake orca/claude recorders and pickup fidelity after source deletion;
  - the install→probe race ONLY if launchd label/plist/socket isolation is proven from source (otherwise no launchctl call at all and an explicit gate);
  - a negative version-skew test against an OLD synckitd (typed "synckitd too old" error, no string matching);
  - status degradation (helper + network shown, delivery marked unavailable).
- (3) An astra review including a safety lens.
Hard safety rules: never touch live daemons/LaunchAgents/~/.claude; no system settings; clean up everything started. Final runs happen on final pins.
